That's all, Mr. Fesini.

01:06:30.030 --> 01:06:32.730
If you want as my countryman that I return to your auditions...

01:06:32.730 --> 01:06:35.230
Yes, I want. I've been a fool.

01:06:35.230 --> 01:06:39.760
In two months, when I finish these contracts, you will return to work for me.

01:06:39.760 --> 01:06:42.710
No, in two months I don't care.

01:06:42.710 --> 01:06:47.990
It must be tomorrow, because tomorrow my mother arrives from Italy and I must receive her as a winner.

01:06:47.990 --> 01:06:50.060
I've written so many letters preparing her.

01:06:50.060 --> 01:06:53.780
Impossible, Nicola. The contracts are serious this time.

01:06:53.780 --> 01:06:58.670
But anyway, I'll talk to Dr. Beragamba tomorrow when you return from Rosario.

01:06:58.670 --> 01:07:00.000
We blow her up!

01:07:00.120 --> 01:07:01.820
He showed up.

01:07:02.140 --> 01:07:03.930
We're dead, Nicora.

01:07:04.130 --> 01:07:05.220
Bad luck.

01:07:05.530 --> 01:07:06.790
Goodbye, Mr. Ferrini.

01:07:07.140 --> 01:07:09.140
Goodbye, gentlemen of the Creole.

01:07:10.560 --> 01:07:12.800
This song has made me cry.

01:07:13.130 --> 01:07:14.630
We're going to continue the session.

01:07:16.640 --> 01:07:19.040
I'm going to continue with the reading of the act.

01:07:20.260 --> 01:07:26.720
Gentlemen, Cortinati, Cappellari, Beccamorti, Capobianca.

01:07:28.590 --> 01:07:29.860
And? How was it?

01:07:30.160 --> 01:07:33.440
Okay, okay. Two months, I don't care.

01:07:34.220 --> 01:07:38.360
- Mom will be here tomorrow. - And I'd like to see her in the auditorium!

01:07:39.500 --> 01:07:42.680
Look, invite her to the orchestra and the other show.

01:07:42.880 --> 01:07:47.180
I have a friend who's a big fan of yours and he's going to play for you.

01:07:47.260 --> 01:07:50.140
I'll wait for you tomorrow at 8:30 p.m. on the radio in Punto.

01:07:50.340 --> 01:07:52.840
- Go! - These delays on the boat.

01:07:53.260 --> 01:07:56.680
- Will Mom come on time to hear me sing? - Of course she will.

01:07:56.760 --> 01:08:00.000
- Be careful. - And you know what happens with the ships. Your mom was going to...

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:04.000
He's not going to be here until 6:00 p.m. He's going to be here until 8:00 p.m. If we don't have time to get to the radio station.

01:08:04.000 --> 01:08:07.750
Don't forget that Hector recommended that we get there at 8:30 p.m.

01:08:07.750 --> 01:08:13.770
Also, the hotel manager has kindly sent a employee to the port with his interpreter to receive his mother.

01:08:13.770 --> 01:08:19.620
You start singing at 8:00 p.m. At that time your old lady will be standing there like a queen in her auditorium.

01:08:19.620 --> 01:08:24.620
Finish getting ready because it's 8:00 p.m. Take it. Grab your baggage, we have to weigh 10 kilos. Take it. Go, go.

01:08:24.620 --> 01:08:29.640
And now we will begin the extraordinary Ferrini and Company program.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:37.510
the soprano Lina Gorgorini and the famous flamenco singer Chabalillo de Triana will act in it,

01:08:37.510 --> 01:08:40.050
with Teres the soprano Gorgorini.

01:09:13.760 --> 01:09:16.200
How am I going to do that? Mr. Ferrini is going to kill me!

01:09:16.200 --> 01:09:19.000
You are the admirer of Nicola Paoni and you have to sing tonight.

01:09:19.000 --> 01:09:21.000
Ferrini is going to thank you in the end.

01:09:21.000 --> 01:09:23.000
How are you going to compare Paoni to that?

01:09:23.000 --> 01:09:27.590
With that?

01:09:27.590 --> 01:09:30.000
Tonight I don't feel very well.

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:33.560
- Thank you, Joel! - Well, what do you want me to do?

01:09:33.560 --> 01:09:38.840
Very simple. When you're announcing Gaita, drop some of this stuff on your microphone.

01:09:38.840 --> 01:09:42.820
- And what's that? - Something harmless, to make you look cool.

01:09:42.820 --> 01:09:45.040
Look.

01:09:45.040 --> 01:09:50.120
But that's outrageous! What if Paone doesn't come and the audition is interrupted?

01:09:50.120 --> 01:09:52.440
Paone is about to come and the orchestra is ready.

01:09:52.440 --> 01:09:54.370
He wants to sing for his wife, who's coming today.

01:09:54.370 --> 01:09:59.510
- You're not playing for a friend. - I'm playing, give it to me.

01:10:11.870 --> 01:10:13.320
This stupid program.

01:10:13.320 --> 01:10:15.060
It looks like a pig they are about to slaughter.

01:10:15.060 --> 01:10:17.420
It's a true manifestation of art.

01:10:17.420 --> 01:10:20.080
How different from when we had Paona.

01:10:20.080 --> 01:10:21.480
He was an artist.

01:10:21.480 --> 01:10:24.770
But because of the intrigues of this man, we lost him.

01:10:24.770 --> 01:10:26.960
Sorry, it was the comment of the people.

01:10:26.960 --> 01:10:28.680
Don't talk about the matter anymore.

01:10:28.680 --> 01:10:30.000
In two months,

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:32.530
We'll have Nicola in the microphone again.

01:10:32.950 --> 01:10:35.990
After the soprano, you'll hear my new discovery.

01:10:36.120 --> 01:10:38.260
- Triana's "Chavalillo". - "Chaval".

01:10:38.550 --> 01:10:40.850
But look at this crap of a name!

01:10:41.800 --> 01:10:43.250
After a short break,

01:10:43.520 --> 01:10:47.340
the soprano Lina Gorgorini will act with us again.

01:10:47.690 --> 01:10:51.200
But first, some advice from our companion Clarita.

01:10:56.480 --> 01:10:59.730
- My mother must be at the stage. - She must be about to arrive, don't hurry.

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:02.560
I wish I had done all this for her if it hadn't come in time.

01:11:02.560 --> 01:11:04.260
I'm going to take a look to see if it's on the stage.

01:11:04.260 --> 01:11:05.760
Very well, thank you, Mr. Ector.

01:11:05.760 --> 01:11:06.960
It's a phenomenon, Mr. Ector.

01:11:06.960 --> 01:11:08.000
Thank you, comrade.

01:11:08.000 --> 01:11:08.600
Open it.

01:11:08.600 --> 01:11:11.000
And now, the sensation of the year.

01:11:11.000 --> 01:11:12.780
"El Chabalillo de Triana."

01:11:12.780 --> 01:11:14.980
He makes his debut tonight on this broadcast

01:11:14.980 --> 01:11:17.860
with an effort of Ferrini and company.

01:11:17.860 --> 01:11:20.640
To make the apology of this gypsy singer,

01:11:20.640 --> 01:11:23.260
imagine that he has traveled the whole world.

01:11:23.260 --> 01:11:25.220
He has traveled all of Spain.

01:11:25.220 --> 01:11:26.420
And also, all of Spain.

01:11:26.420 --> 01:11:27.560
What do I say? Spain!

01:11:27.560 --> 01:11:28.670
He has walked through France...

01:11:28.670 --> 01:11:30.000
Don't let me finish.

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:32.030
I'm not playing around here, I'm just coming.

01:11:32.130 --> 01:11:41.630
Let's see how you do today.

01:11:41.730 --> 01:11:46.030
- Come on, move. - I lost my hand.

01:11:46.130 --> 01:11:48.330
- With nerves, I broke half of it. - Better.

01:11:48.430 --> 01:11:51.030
Now be careful to change the microphone for when Paone sings.

01:11:51.130 --> 01:11:56.630
- Yes, man, yes. - Paone!

01:11:56.730 --> 01:12:00.000
I didn't know you were going to work. I accidentally saved him...

01:12:00.320 --> 01:12:01.820
I don't want it, but 15 days.

01:12:01.920 --> 01:12:02.820
- For me? - Yes.

01:12:02.920 --> 01:12:04.010
Any other advice?

01:12:04.110 --> 01:12:07.110
It must be that lioness of Villa Soldati who always writes to you.

01:12:07.210 --> 01:12:09.810
I spent a night in Triana!

01:12:09.830 --> 01:12:12.230
- I'm so scared! - It doesn't work!

01:12:12.820 --> 01:12:15.780
A second more, and I'm going to buy pepper!

01:12:15.780 --> 01:12:18.120
Oh, no!

01:12:18.350 --> 01:12:19.720
Oh, no!

01:12:20.190 --> 01:12:21.920
Or not?

01:12:31.020 --> 01:12:34.520
- What a scandal! - I don't know. He must have been constipated.

01:12:34.620 --> 01:12:36.220
Let's go to the radio, dad. The car is downstairs.

01:12:36.320 --> 01:12:38.040
- Go out, I'm going to look for the door. - Yes.

01:12:42.120 --> 01:12:44.440
Dear radio listeners.

01:12:44.600 --> 01:12:48.980
A sudden cold prevents Triana's great brother-in-law from acting tonight.

01:12:49.260 --> 01:12:53.160
But since he happens to be visiting the house, the great Nicola Paone,

01:12:53.260 --> 01:12:55.380
he will kindly take his place.

01:12:58.110 --> 01:13:00.000
Now it's your turn, Paone's wife.

01:13:00.480 --> 01:13:01.800
Let's see how he behaves, eh?

01:13:01.920 --> 01:13:03.880
Go to the microphone, I'm going to see it from here, take it.

01:13:04.080 --> 01:13:05.030
Of course I'm going.

01:13:09.360 --> 01:13:10.150
Kind...

01:13:11.020 --> 01:13:12.100
...Casimensarco.

01:13:14.440 --> 01:13:16.080
Kind radio listeners...

01:13:16.280 --> 01:13:17.840
...do not believe they have lost the night...

01:13:18.040 --> 01:13:22.160
...because they are going to listen again to the formidable troubadour of Italy...

01:13:22.360 --> 01:13:23.880
...Nicola Pa...

01:13:25.700 --> 01:13:27.490
Ah! Ah!

01:13:38.860 --> 01:13:40.760
- Take him away! - No, don't do that!

01:13:42.990 --> 01:13:44.990
- Take him away! - Take him away!

01:13:46.130 --> 01:13:49.330
Miss Diximula, Diximula, nothing has happened, calm down, please.

01:13:49.330 --> 01:13:51.330
Yes, help, help him get up.

01:13:51.330 --> 01:13:54.340
Yes, that lady, please. Yes, the lady and the children first.

01:13:54.340 --> 01:13:57.640
Yes, now he's going to be with you again, the great Nicola Paone.

01:13:57.640 --> 01:14:00.000
Come on, Paone. But please, calm down.

01:14:00.220 --> 01:14:04.420
A letter from his sister announcing the death of his mother.

01:14:04.420 --> 01:14:07.200
Poor thing, he shouldn't sing.

01:14:07.200 --> 01:14:08.960
And what do we do now if he doesn't sing?

01:14:08.960 --> 01:14:10.210
Everything has been useless.

01:14:10.210 --> 01:14:11.450
Let's take him to the hotel.

01:14:11.450 --> 01:14:12.640
Let's go, Nicolás.

01:14:12.640 --> 01:14:14.680
No, I have to sing.

01:14:14.680 --> 01:14:16.260
The audience is waiting for me.

01:14:16.260 --> 01:14:19.030
And besides, I have something to tell you.

01:14:19.030 --> 01:14:26.670
Now? But how did he get in here?

01:14:26.670 --> 01:14:27.870
What does he want to talk about?

01:14:27.870 --> 01:14:30.000
Ladies and gentlemen...

01:14:30.410 --> 01:14:34.010
This whole thing that happened here tonight is because my mother from Italy should have come.

01:14:34.710 --> 01:14:36.210
And I wanted to deceive her.

01:14:36.680 --> 01:14:39.300
I wanted her to see me triumph once more.

01:14:39.410 --> 01:14:41.910
- Don't sing, Nicola. - Yes, I have to sing.

01:14:42.650 --> 01:14:45.430
Because I promised her a new song for tonight.

01:14:46.130 --> 01:14:49.720
And she's from heaven. I'm sure I want to hear it.

01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:01.000
Cue Cue Cue

01:15:01.000 --> 01:15:03.640
Paisano how are you?

01:15:03.640 --> 01:15:05.640
Cue Paisano how are you?

01:15:05.640 --> 01:15:10.410
Italy is small, there are people in quantity

01:15:10.410 --> 01:15:14.380
This is the ruin that you can not camp

01:15:14.380 --> 01:15:18.120
Everyone must go abroad, you know

01:15:18.120 --> 01:15:21.620
To earn some bread for dad and mom

01:15:21.620 --> 01:15:25.630
And leave the family, from home you go

01:15:25.630 --> 01:15:30.000
Earn the bread yes, but lose the happiness

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:34.340
- -

01:15:34.340 --> 01:15:38.200
- -

01:15:38.200 --> 01:15:42.050
- -

01:15:42.050 --> 01:15:45.000
- -

01:15:45.030 --> 01:15:53.190
When he meets an Italian, go and shake his hand, because he will rejoice.

01:15:53.190 --> 01:15:58.340
And he says: "Hue, peasant!" "Hue, peasant!"

01:15:58.340 --> 01:15:59.340
"Inchostro, cartel!"

01:16:00.220 --> 01:16:06.400
My dear mother, I'm very well here, don't worry.

01:16:06.400 --> 01:16:09.960
Tell me how you are and how your father is.

01:16:09.960 --> 01:16:13.440
Please answer, don't make me wait.

01:16:13.440 --> 01:16:18.180
And wait, wait, one day a letter comes in,

01:16:18.180 --> 01:16:25.590
and a sister writes that there is no longer a mother.

01:16:25.590 --> 01:16:28.160
What a peasant!

01:16:28.160 --> 01:16:30.000
What a peasant!

01:16:34.350 --> 01:16:54.880
I think what I say is true.

01:16:54.880 --> 01:16:59.440
Well, well, well.

01:17:11.130 --> 01:17:12.970
- Cry, Dad. - And to me.

01:17:13.030 --> 01:17:18.100
- You are weak. - What a scandal!

01:17:18.200 --> 01:17:20.480
You can't miss five minutes without making a mess!

01:17:20.530 --> 01:17:23.310
What will Mr. Parrilli say? Get out of here!

01:17:23.390 --> 01:17:24.750
- Wait a minute! - Help him, Dad.

01:17:24.850 --> 01:17:28.580
I didn't know that man's drama.

01:17:30.410 --> 01:17:32.710
I'm sorry, Mr. Ferrini. I left the station a moment ago and...

01:17:32.730 --> 01:17:36.540
On the contrary. Now I understand that I've been an idiot.

01:17:36.920 --> 01:17:38.080
Give me that hand, peasant.

01:17:38.520 --> 01:17:41.160
From now on, you'll be my main number again.

01:17:41.540 --> 01:17:42.750
Thank you so much.

01:17:42.770 --> 01:17:45.410
But now, what's the point of the triumph?

01:17:46.120 --> 01:17:49.640
I feel so lonely. I won't sing anymore.

01:17:49.930 --> 01:17:51.920
No, Nicola. You won't be alone.

01:17:52.690 --> 01:17:54.010
I'll always be with you.

01:17:55.010 --> 01:17:56.550
Forgive my stupid pride of before.

01:17:58.110 --> 01:18:00.000
But, at this time, you...

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:03.810
Yes, Nicola. I think I've known you since.

01:18:03.890 --> 01:18:06.340
For your manliness and kindness.

01:18:06.420 --> 01:18:10.410
Then, with you by my side, the world is mine.

01:18:10.490 --> 01:18:12.050
I'll sing for you.

01:18:12.130 --> 01:18:13.980
Thank you so much, Mr. Ferrin.

01:18:14.060 --> 01:18:15.060
Just a moment!

01:18:16.060 --> 01:18:18.810
Don't be afraid, gentlemen.

01:18:18.890 --> 01:18:19.810
It's already happened to me.

01:18:19.880 --> 01:18:22.190
This doesn't fail any American movie.

01:18:22.270 --> 01:18:25.330
Now the number is going to cost you double, Mr. Ferrin.

01:18:25.410 --> 01:18:26.920
Let's not talk about money.

01:18:27.000 --> 01:18:30.000
What happens to me is that when I meet someone, I say:

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:31.860
with Mr. Ferrini and tell me:

01:18:31.940 --> 01:18:34.480
"Oh, oh, oh, oh, Baetano!"
